  "decision_conditions": [
    "On the basis of the evidence submitted and on the balance of\nprobabilities, the use of the existing property as a House of Multiple Occupation\n(HMO) for up to 7 (seven) persons (Use Class: Sui Generis) was in situ and in\nuse for a continuous period of at least 4 years prior to the date of this\napplication. The 7 bedroom HMO is therefore immune from enforcement action\nunder S.171B of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and is\nlawful under Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as\namended)."
